"Young wizards earn provisional, monitored summoning rights some years into adulthood."
"Summoning rights can be revoked completely."
"A young wizard needs formal permission and mentor oversight even to talk with an Avowed."
"Titles like Distinguished can be officially stripped from a disgraced wizard."
"Wizards must earn summoning rights for each species; newcomers to Earth may lack them for humans."
"Giving a Ryeh-b't inappropriate tasks brings zealous scrutiny if complaints or injuries follow."
"Such scrutiny threatens a wizard's summoning rights; Contracts may still pick anyone for emergencies."
"A commendation makes inappropriate summons of its holder vanishingly unlikely."
"Some Rapportfolk who summon casually will not call humans unless their service is irreplaceable."
